# Maze of Ith: "{T}: Untap target attacking creature. Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt to and dealt by that
# creature this turn." Bot1 attacks with Guerrilla Gorilla (2/2); Llanowar Elves stays home. Bot2 blocks with its own
# Gorilla. In the declare blockers step Bot2 can't target the Elves, which is not attacking (the positive control is the
# attacking Gorilla), and Mazes the attacking Gorilla: it untaps, stays in combat and blocked (the rulings), and neither the
# 2 it would deal nor the 2 the blocker would deal it is dealt (CR 615.1) - each recorded as Maze of Ith's. Both Gorillas
# survive undamaged and Bot2 takes nothing.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Guerrilla Gorilla
Llanowar Elves
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Maze of Ith
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
